  'flashing-repairs': { title: 'JUNCTIONS DESERVE THEIR OWN NOTES.', eyebrow: 'FLASHING / PRACTICAL NOTES', intro: 'Flashing is used where roof materials meet walls, openings or other changes in plane, making precise location especially useful.', signs: 'Look for lifted edges, gaps, staining near a junction, or changes around chimneys, skylights, walls and penetrations.', context: 'A flashing detail guides water through a transition rather than acting alone. The adjoining roof material and drainage direction matter too.', nextStep: 'Describe the nearby feature and whether the observation changes after rain or wind.', guide: '/news/roof-flashing-explained/', guideLabel: 'Read the guide to roof flashing' },
